1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,940
Good morning. How can I help you?

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:05,900
Hello. I'm interested in renting a house somewhere in the town.

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:09,000
Right. Could I have your name please?

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,920
Yes, it's Steven Godfrey.

5
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:14,960
And tell me how many bedrooms you're looking for.

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:19,930
Well, we'd need four, because I'm going to share the house with three friends.

7
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:23,540
Okay, there are several of that size on our books.

8
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:26,760
They mostly belong to families who are working abroad at the moment.

9
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,850
What about the location?

10
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:31,400
It'd be nice to be central.

11
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:35,920
That might be difficult, as most houses of that size are in the suburbs.

12
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:40,760
Still, there are a few. What's your upper limit for the rent?

13
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:47,278
We'd like something around £500 a month, but we could go up to £600 if we have to.

14
00:00:47,278 --> 00:00:49,450
But we can't go beyond that.

15
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:53,400
Do you know how long you want to rent the house for?

16
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,310
The minimum let is six months, as you probably realise.

17
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:58,880
We're at college here for two years

18
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:02,360
and we don't want to have to move during that time if we can avoid it.

19
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:06,000
Right. And how soon do you want to move in

20
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,380
All our lets start on the first of the month.

21
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:13,000
Well, as soon as possible, really, so that means September 1st.

22
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,040
Okay, let me have a look at what we've got We have photographs of all the houses on our books,

23
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:20,560
so you can get an idea of what they're like.

24
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:25,425
There's this one in Oakington Avenue, at £550 a month.

25
00:01:25,425 --> 00:01:30,290
Combined living room and dining room, with a separate kitchen.

26
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:33,930
It doesn't have a garage, though you can park in the road.

27
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:36,920
Ah, we'd prefer to have one, if possible.

28
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:41,860
Right. Then have a look at this house, in Mead Street.

29
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:46,200
It's got a very large living room and kitchen, bathroom, cloakroom...

30
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:46,850
How much is it?

31
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:51,680
That one's 580. It's very well furnished and equipped.

32
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:57,039
It also has plenty of space for parking, and it's available for a minimum of a year.

33
00:01:57,039 --> 00:01:58,930
Oh, and there's a big garden.

34
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:01,780
I don't think we could cope with that, to be honest

35
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,730
We'll be too busy to look after it.

36
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:08,423
Okay. Then there's this older house in Hamilton Road:

37
00:02:08,423 --> 00:02:14,160
living room, kitchen-diner, and it has a study. 550 a month.

38
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:18,200
That looks rather nice. But whereabouts in Hamilton Road?

39
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,270
Towards the western end.

40
00:02:20,270 --> 00:02:23,410
Oh, that'll be very noisy. I know the area.

41
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:26,740
Yes, it's pretty lively. Some people like it, though

42
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:31,530
Well, what about this house in Devon Close?

43
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:33,030
That looks lovely.

44
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:37,360
There's a big demand for houses in that area, so prices tend to be quite high.

45
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,400
But this one hasn't been decorated for a few years

46
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,590
which has kept the rent down a bit.

47
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:47,362
It's got a living room, dining room and small kitchen, and it's 595 a month.

48
00:02:47,362 --> 00:02:51,210
I think it would suit you, from what you've said.

49
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,710
It sounds fine.

50
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:55,750
Why's that part of town so popular?

51
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:58,500
Well, there's a big scheme to improve the district

52
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:01,100
and it'll soon have the best facilities for miles around.

53
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,290
What sort of thing?

54
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:04,820
There's a big sports centre under construction

55
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,770
which will be very impressive when it's finished.

56
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:09,600
In fact the swimming pool's already opened

57
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,450
ahead of schedule, and it's attracting a lot of people.

58
00:03:12,450 --> 00:03:15,520
What about cinemas: are there any in the area?

59
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:18,060
The only one closed down last year

60
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:21,160
and it's now in the process of being converted into a film museum.

61
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:24,970
The local people are trying to get a new cinema added to the scheme.

62
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:30,830
I think I heard something about a plan to replace the existing concert hall with a larger one.

63
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:33,630
Ah, that's due to start next year.

64
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:38,320
Well it sounds an interesting area to live in. Could I go and see the house, please?

65
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,200
Yes, of course.
